  "comment": "KOJ judge seccomp profile. Vendored snapshot derived from the Docker/Moby default seccomp profile (defaultAction SCMP_ACT_ERRNO, fail-closed). NOT a hand-rolled minimal allowlist: dangerous syscalls (mount/umount/pivot_root, reboot, swapon/swapoff, init/delete_module, kexec, open_by_handle_at, clock_settime/adjtime, ptrace, personality, bpf, io_uring, userfaultfd, perf_event_open, keyctl) are omitted on purpose so they fail with ERRNO, preserving Docker default protections. Provision this file to the judge host at /etc/koj/seccomp-koj.json (see api/DEPLOYMENT_CONTRACT.md). The judge passes --security-opt seccomp=/etc/koj/seccomp-koj.json on every docker run and fails closed when the daemon rejects a missing/invalid profile. Review against the pinned Moby default before changing; do not claim an exhaustive audit.",
